# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# prefs: factory
# setup: benchpast
# board: only
# What a suite last did here, said where it is being decided.
#
# The bench keeps a ledger of its own runs; the shell only says what is
# in it, at the moment somebody is looking at a suite and deciding
# whether to run it again.  Two answers matter and they are different:
# what it did last time, and that it has never been done here at all.
wait 60
click 980 30
wait 10
menu-pick Applications
wait 10
menu-pick Bench
wait 250
expect-title Bench
click-window Bench
wait 8
note the top row is the kernel suite, which HAS run on this board
key Down
wait 8
click 71 8
wait 8
note the authoritative full run only: a part of a suite passing says
note nothing about the suite
expect-menu kernel on tiku: FAILED
note and a suite that has never run here says exactly that, which is not
note the same answer as a pass
click-window Bench
wait 8
key Down
wait 3
key Down
wait 3
key Down
wait 3
key Down
wait 3
key Down
wait 3
key Down
wait 3
key Down
wait 3
wait 8
click 71 8
wait 8
expect-menu link-console has not run here
quit
